<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assab Bay</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Assab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Assab Bay is a bay on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>. An Italian shipping company acquired land there in 1869, and the Italian state took it over in 1882. It was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s first colonial foothold in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and the starting point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>, later expanded into the colony of Eritrea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assab-bay.jpg" alt="Assab Bay" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: vxr7475 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B5%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%A9_%D9%83%D9%86%D9%8A%D8%B3%D8%A9_%D9%81%D9%8A_%D8%B9%D8%B5%D8%A8_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
